From 92b271fa2aa0071d461d9071a6b8ef1b4207030d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:02:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/45] Reconstruct the TCP socket-buffer helpers

tcp_sb.c is split out of the public tcp_subr.c in the reference.
Recover tcp_sbrcv_min_rwin from the public tcp_sbrcv_grow_rwin body
(the reference renamed it) and point tcp_sbspace at it; the function
is static per the DWARF.

Mark tcp_sbrcv_grow, tcp_sbrcv_trim, tcp_sbrcv_tstmp_check and
tcp_sbsnd_trim external, move their prototypes to tcp_var.h, and drop
the stale tcp_input.c prototypes and the now-unused
tcp_sbrcv_grow_rwin definition from tcp_subr.c.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
 bsd/netinet/tcp_input.c |  7 ------
 bsd/netinet/tcp_sb.c    | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 bsd/netinet/tcp_subr.c  | 31 ------------------------
 bsd/netinet/tcp_var.h   |  5 ++++
 4 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

